# Project rules

- Use C++20, Qt 6.12 Widgets, Visual Studio 2022 and MSBuild.
- Consult Context7 and official Qt 6.12 documentation when unsure about Qt APIs.
- Prefer official documentation: https://doc.qt.io/qt-6.12/
- Never invent Qt classes, methods or properties.
- Use the existing ui/MainWindow.ui for the main interface. Keep headers in include/, sources in src/, and QSS plus icons in resources/.
- Use custom QWidget components for dynamic application cards.
- Use QPainter for the circular progress indicator.
- Use Qt layouts instead of absolute positioning.
- Use QSS for visual styling where appropriate.
- Do not introduce QML, Qt Quick, CMake or third-party UI frameworks.
- Follow existing C++ formatting and naming conventions.
- Keep ApplicationCore, WingetPoC and ApplicationGUI separated.
- Do not modify backend code during UI-only tasks.
- Do not change project configuration or dependencies unnecessarily.
- Ensure new files are included in the existing Qt/MSBuild project.
- Build and check for compilation errors after changes.
